      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The authors' claim of state-of-the-art status relies heavily on a multi-head attention mechanism, yet their ablation study fails to demonstrate that temporal dependency capture actually exceeds simpler baselines like TCN or Dilated Convolution. Without explicitly isolating how the number of attention heads influences performance on varying temporal resolution, it is difficult to attribute gains solely to the Transformer architecture rather than standard hyperparameter tuning. This lack of granular methodological breakdown obscures whether the model's superior MSE and MAE results stem from genuine architectural innovation or robust baseline fitting. Consequently, while the experimental setup is sound, the inability to rigorously justify the reliance on attention mechanisms over established temporal models leaves critical questions about the model's generalizability and true marginal contribution unanswered.",
      "source": "target",
